# E20 RemoteMessages over the ActressMAS transport, with a server that may swap two messages of a container: the C#
# server relays each message on a thread of its pool, so the two answers of the pong agent may reach Container1 in either
# order, in the C# as in the C++. The messages received are compared as a multiset, each with its sender
# "name@container"; everything else as in RemoteMessages.actressmas.rules.
section ^This is Container\d$
ignore ^$
ignore ^Container connecting to server\.\.\.$
ignore ^Container connected to server\.$
ignore ^Container\d registered\.$
ignore ^Running MAS\.\.\.$
cover all
fact setup ^\[(ping-agent|pong-agent)\] (.+)$
fact received ^\t\[(\S+) -> (ping-agent|pong-agent)\]: (.+)$
same setup seq by 0
same received bag
check setup count == 2
check received count == 3
